LineageGuard:

```java
@Component
public class LineageGuard {
    private final BatchRepository repo;
    public void assertNoRecalledAncestor(String batchKey) { ... }
    public Optional<String> recalledAncestor(String batchKey) { ... }
    private Map<String,String> childToParent() { ... }
}
```

BatchService will delegate its assertNoRecalledAncestor to the guard. But BatchService also uses recalledAncestor and childToParent privately for listing. I'll keep those private methods in BatchService (duplication acceptable) and just have BatchService.assertNoRecalledAncestor delegate to guard? Simpler: BatchService keeps everything as-is; RecipeService uses LineageGuard. Slight duplication of the guard logic between BatchService private method and LineageGuard. To minimize risk of breaking existing tests, leave BatchService untouched in that respect, and LineageGuard standalone. Fine.

Now RecipeService. Structure:

```java
@Service
public class RecipeService {
    CMD_CREATE_RECIPE, CMD_BIND, CMD_WEIGH, CMD_CORRECT
    MAX_MASS_SCALE=6, MAX_PERCENTAGE_SCALE=4, TOLERANCE = new BigDecimal("0.1"), HUNDRED=100

    deps: RecipeRepository recipes, BatchRepository batches, LineageGuard lineageGuard, TransactionTemplate tx, ObjectMapper objectMapper

    createRecipe(operator, req)
    getRecipe(recipeKey)
    bindRecipe(operator, batchKey, req)
    weigh(operator, batchKey, req)
    correct(operator, batchKey, req)
    status(batchKey)
    assertReleaseReady(batchKey)  // called within BatchService tx
    planSplitInheritance(parentKey, children) // called within split tx
    applySplitInheritance(plan, commandKey, now)
    // helpers: requireOperator, executeIdempotent, structuredFingerprint, validateMass, validatePercentage, computeStatus
}
```

